MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Bruno,

The Pl slot is the marginalized probability of a particular observed response pattern, which is why it changes if your datasets contain different responses. It is paired with the observed responses found in residuals(mod, type = 'exp', digits = Inf), where the Pl values are multiplied by N to obtain the expected values. Dividing the $exp element by the sample size will give you the same values in @Pl. Cheers.

Phil

